Freeze-bout probes (this bout, executed fresh): `tmp/phase3-b2/probe_freeze.rb`
(receipt `tmp/phase3-b2/receipts/probe-freeze.out`) and
`tmp/phase3-b2/probe_cast_bool.rb` (receipt
`tmp/phase3-b2/receipts/probe-cast-bool.out`). Findings folded into the
decisions below:

- `cast: :to_b` does NOT exist in the loaded stack (`NoMethodError:
  undefined method 'to_b' for an instance of String` when the parser
  applies it) — booleans are pinned as strings (receipts
  `tmp/phase3-b2/receipts/probe-cast-bool.out` and probe-freeze A).
- UTC `iso8601(3)` timestamps: lexical sort == chronological sort on a
  5-point sample spanning years; no TAB/NEWLINE/CR inside; a
  `+01:00`-offset input normalizes to `...Z`. WRITER-SIDE PARSER NOTE
  (folded in during implementation): Ruby's `Time.parse` on an
  ISO-8601-with-milliseconds string DROPS the fractional seconds
  (`Time.parse("2026-02-03T12:00:00.500+01:00")` =>
  `11:00:00.000Z`); `Time.iso8601` keeps them. The frozen timestamp
  encoder therefore uses Time objects directly, then strict
  `Time.iso8601`, then lenient `Time.parse` as the last resort; the
  millisecond-truncation behavior is pinned by test.
- A literal `\N` cell round-trips verbatim and stays distinct from an
  empty cell after `TSV.open` (both in `:list` tables).
- Registering the same annotation name twice via `TSV.annotation` is
  harmless (dump and reopen unaffected); registration is idempotent in
  effect. (Folded in during implementation, probe D of
  probe_freeze.rb.)
- Cast `:to_i` empty cell -> nil, re-confirmed.

## 1. Global encoding rules (apply to every task below)

### 1a. Entity-ID grammar

Escaping table (applied to PATH COMPONENTS of every identifier and to
every path-valued key or cell; single-pass, no re-scanning):

| raw character | escape |
|---|---|
| `%` | `%25` |
| `#` | `%23` |
| TAB | `%09` |
| NEWLINE | `%0A` |
| CR | `%0D` |

CR is INCLUDED (decision 1c of stage-0 §4, direction accepted): TSV holds
CR verbatim, but a one-character-symmetry escape costs nothing and removes
a whole class of CR/LF-normalization accidents at file boundaries. The
table is closed: no other character is escaped, and `%` sequences not in
the table are left alone on unescape only in their exact table spellings
(unescape recognizes exactly `%25 %23 %09 %0A %0D`).

Identifier forms:

- **Chat** = absolute canonical chat path, `Chat.provenance_path(:chat,
  ...)` spelling (the EXISTING canonical form; no new canonical spelling
  is invented). The `/home`-vs-`/bulk` device-tree fact documented in
  `test/test_canonical_paths.rb` stays as-is: they are different device
  trees, only this checkout is bind-mounted at the `/bulk` spelling, and
  `Chat.provenance_path` resolves to whichever spelling the running
  process's canonicalization yields. In TSV cells/keys the path is
  escaped per the table.
- **Job** = absolute canonical job path (`Chat.provenance_path(:job,
  step)` spelling). A DISTINCT entity type from Chat even when a
  chat-producing job and its output chat share one path (the overview
  visited-set already keys on the kind pair).
- **Message** = `escaped_chat_path + '#' + decimal_index`, zero-based
  index into that chat's parsed message sequence. The separator is the
  LAST raw `#` possible only because the path is escaped (a raw `#`
  cannot survive in the path part); splitting the whole id on `#` yields
  exactly two parts for a plain message id.
- **Inference** = the Message id of its meta message (one inference per
  meta message).
- **Tool call** = the Message id of its call-start message
  (function_call / mcp_call).
- **Activity cluster** = the Message id of its FIRST inference (see 1h;
  scoped by root + max_gap_seconds, not persistent across parameter
  changes — re-derivable, never stored as an identity).
- **Token event** = the event's core identity rendered as
  `escaped(identity parts).join('#')` — e.g. `inference_id#w1`,
  `provider_response_id#resp_1`, `lineage#L47`, `receipt#<escaped
  evidence_address>`. The identity Array is the core's grouping key
  (scout-ai provenance/tokens.rb), so it is unique per deduplicated
  event; each element is path-escaped before joining (the 1a CLOSED
  table: `#`/`%`/TAB/NEWLINE/CR — NOT URL encoding; `|`, `~`, space
  stay literal), so an evidence address containing `#`/`%`/TAB cannot
  corrupt the join.
- **Inbox note** = absolute note path (escaped in cells).

Composite row keys (pairs), all built with the SAME `#` join over escaped
components (key uniqueness is test-enforced):

- (chat, role): `escaped_chat_path + '#' + role`
- (message, reference occurrence):
  `message_id + '#' + reference_type + '#' + occurrence`, occurrence
  1-based among references of the same (message, reference_type), in the
  order the sources yield them (graph array order for job references,
  message order for relationship references). ALWAYS three trailing
  segments — no conditional presence.
  NOTE: `reference_type` itself contains no `#` by construction (it is
  one of the five enumeration values), so the composite grammar stays
  unambiguous; `token_event_id` composites are the general case handled
  by the escaped-token-event-id rule above.
- (call, job): `call_message_id + '#' + escaped_job_path`
- (event, evidence occurrence): `token_event_id + '#' + occurrence`
  (1-based, canonical evidence first).

Because every component is escaped, splitting any composite key on `#`
recovers the parts unambiguously.

### 1b. Null convention (SETTLED — direction accepted)

- String columns: the sentinel `\N` (two characters: backslash, N) means
  NULL. The empty string `""` ALWAYS means empty string, never null.
  Tests must and do distinguish `\N` from `""` after dump/reopen.
- Cast numeric columns (`:to_i`/`:to_f` tables): native empty cell =>
  nil (executed fact, probes C and freeze probe E). No sentinel needed.
- The absent-trailing-cell asymmetry (a `:single` row whose last cell is
  physically absent reads nil) is NEVER relied upon: every table in this
  contract is `:list`, every row is written with ALL cells present.
- The `|` invariant: no `|` inside any multi-value cell (the dumper
  rejoins multi-values with `|`; a `|` inside a value would corrupt
  read-back). Multi-value columns in this contract carry only paths,
  controlled names and enumerations, all `|`-free by construction; the
  writers validate this.

### 1c. Cast rule and boolean encoding (SETTLED)

- Global cast only, Symbol form (`:to_i` / `:to_f`). Per-field Hash cast
  is banned (silently dropped — stage-0 1b).
- A table casts ONLY when EVERY field is numeric. Mixed tables stay
  all-Strings; numeric values in mixed tables are decimal strings
  (`42`, `3.5`, `-1`). Decision 4 of stage-0 §4 accepted: the analytical
  consumer is the ChatAnalyst agent reading TSV text, and decimal-string
  counts are directly comparable; native Integer cells are reserved for
  the purely numeric tables where they are free.
- Booleans: the strings `true` / `false`; NULL is `\N`. There is NO
  `:to_b` cast in the loaded stack (freeze probe A: NoMethodError when
  the parser tries to apply it). No current consumer needs native
  booleans (stage-0 2c: the only consumer is the ChatAnalyst agent
  itself); if one appears later, the read-side helper decodes the
  strings — the encoding does not change.

### 1d. Timestamp format (SETTLED)

UTC ISO 8601 with millisecond precision, `Time#utc.iso8601(3)` — the
SAME spelling the scout-ai core writer uses for meta timestamps
(`Time.now.utc.iso8601(3)`, provenance/live.rb:1077). Verified sortable
(lexical == chronological), TSV-safe (no TAB/NEWLINE/CR), and
normalizing (offset inputs become `Z`). PARSER ORDER (pinned by test
during this bout's implementation): a Time input is used as-is (a
`to_s` round-trip LOSES sub-second precision under the lenient
parser); a String input goes strict `Time.iso8601` FIRST (it preserves
milliseconds where Ruby's lenient `Time.parse` silently drops them),
falling back to lenient `Time.parse` for non-ISO spellings (e.g.
`2026-02-03 12:00:00.500 +0100`). Writers normalize any parseable
input to this form; a missing OR unparseable timestamp becomes NULL
(`\N`) in String tables — the existing `timeline_safe_timestamp`
keep-only-if-parseable policy, with normalization added. Never invent a
timestamp.

### 1e. Allowed cell content (restated from the approved spec)

Allowed: identifiers, paths, controlled enumerations, timestamps,
counts, sizes, token numbers, booleans, foreign keys, short structured
values (tool_name, target_agent, target_conversation). Excluded
everywhere: message bodies, reasoning text, tool argument/output
content, exception messages, note contents, nested structures as
strings. `chat_message`/`chat_range` (`:chat` outputs) and `inbox_note`
(`:text` output) are the ONLY body-carrying surfaces, by design.

### 1f. Pagination and metadata annotations

Mechanism (stage-0 settled 3): module-level `TSV.annotation` DSL;
registered once at library load (see 1g); values ride the `#:` line and
survive both `TSV.open` and task persistence (`Step#load.load`).
Scalar values only; no TAB/NEWLINE inside annotation strings; an absent
directive means nil (correct for next_page/prev_page). CRITICAL SAFETY
RULE discovered during this bout's implementation: a raw `#` inside an
annotation VALUE corrupts the `#:`-line grammar (the directives are
`#:`-joined), so every PATH-valued annotation carries the ESCAPED
canonical path (the 1a escape table removes `#`, TAB and NEWLINE, which
is exactly the set the annotation line cannot hold).

Pagination semantics (unchanged from the current JSON envelope): the
inputs `page` (1-based Integer) and `per_page` (Integer, default 50,
minimum 1) exist on every task marked "paginated"; pagination is APPLIED
only when `page` is given; page bounds the main list only, never totals;
out-of-range page yields an empty row set, not an error; `total` always
counts the unpaginated universe.

Registered annotation names (complete list — additions beyond the
settled DSL set are marked and justified):

| name | used by | justification |
|---|---|---|
| `page`, `per_page`, `total`, `total_pages`, `next_page`, `prev_page` | every paginated task | settled DSL set |
| `root_path` | every rooted task | settled DSL set |
| `max_gap_seconds` | cluster tasks | settled DSL set |
| `first`, `last` | chat_range, chat_message | ADDITION: a `:chat` output carries no envelope; without these the slice loses its addressing. Escaped path goes in `root_path`; indices here. |
| `scope` | chat_accounting | ADDITION: distinguishes own/closure result shape of the same task name. |
| `filters` | chat_tool_calls | ADDITION: comma-joined `k=v` list of applied filters so the artifact self-describes which subset it holds. |
| `chats`, `jobs`, `delegations` | chat_overview | ADDITION: summary counts (decision 3 below). |
| `clusters`, `inferences`, `unclustered` | chat_activity_clusters | ADDITION: summary counts (decision 3 below). |
| `conflicts`, `incomplete_evidence` | chat_tokens | ADDITION: token-summary quality flags the JSON surface carried; they are scalars and belong with the summary. |

### 1g. Annotation-registration placement

`lib/ChatAnalyst/tsv_base.rb` registers ALL names from 1f via one
`TSV.annotation` call at load. It is required from `workflow.rb`
immediately after `ChatAnalyst/api` (and therefore before any task file
that builds tables), so every task run and every test that loads the
workflow — test_helper requires workflow.rb — sees the accessors.
Duplicate registration is harmless (freeze probe C). The full registered
list is the 1f table (19 names). `TSV.parse_header` remains the
registration-free fallback reader for consumers outside the workflow.

### 1h. Activity-cluster model (contract for plan step 3; AMENDED bout 3, C1)

An activity cluster is a maximal run of CONSECUTIVE TIMESTAMPED
inferences (in the chronologically sorted, tree-wide inference sequence)
whose adjacent gaps are at most `max_gap_seconds`. Missing-timestamp
policy (C1 amendment; the user-approved spec is authoritative over the
frozen text here): ONLY timestamped inferences participate in
clustering. An inference whose timestamp is missing/unparseable joins
NO cluster, carries NO `activity_cluster_id` (the `\N` null in the
TSV), and influences no gap computation — it never bridges two distant
clusters. `unclustered` is a real, possibly-nonzero count of exactly
these inferences. Cluster id = Message id of the cluster's first
inference. Clusters are scoped by (root, max_gap_seconds) and are never
persisted as identities.
`chat_activity_cluster` MUST reuse `chat_activity_clusters`' computation
through a Scout task dependency (`dep ... step(:chat_activity_clusters)
.load`), never recompute independently — the same-clustering-validation
requirement of the spec.

## 2. Task surface (frozen)

Notation per task: inputs (name: type, default); output kind; key_field;
fields with per-field encoding; pagination; annotations; FK columns;
null policy beyond the global rules. "int-str" = decimal string in an
all-String table; "int" = native via table-wide cast. All `file` inputs
are `:path`, required, jobname; pagination inputs as in 1f. Rooted tasks
carry `root_path`; every table carries `total` when paginated and may
carry it unpaginated (writers always set it — a table's row count is
cheap and self-describing).

### A. Overview and relationship tables

**chat_overview** — converted in place from JSON (same name).
- Inputs: `file: path (required)`, `root_type: string, nil`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `Chat`, cast none (mixed).
- Fields per chat row: `messages` int-str; `references` int-str (count of
  provenance references: job references + delegations; relationship
  references import/continue/last are NOT included — they belong to
  chat_references); `warnings` int-str.
- No pagination (one row per chat of the tree; bounded by tree size).
- Annotations: `root_path`, `total`, `chats`, `jobs`, `delegations`
  (summary counts: chats = row count, jobs = jobs in tree, delegations =
  delegation references across chats — all derived by the traversal it
  already performs; decision 3).
- FK: key -> Chat.

**job_overview** — NEW.
- Inputs: `file: path (required)`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `Job`, cast none.
- Fields: `result_chat` escaped path or `\N` (no chat-typed result);
  `dependency_count` int-str; `live_log_count` int-str.
- No pagination. Annotations: `root_path`, `total`.
- FK: key -> Job; `result_chat` -> Chat.

**chat_references** — NEW (absorbs the references the old chat_overview
JSON embedded plus relationship references).
- Inputs: `file: path (required)` (chat file).
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list` (aligned-by-construction per stage-0
  settled 1 — the `one2one` decision), key_field `Reference` = composite
  `message_id#reference_type#occurrence`, cast none.
- Fields: `source_message_id` (Message FK; redundant with key by design —
  alignment), `reference_type` enumeration `job_reference | delegation |
  import | continue | last` (SETTLED: the two core kinds `dependencies`
  and `live` are EXCLUDED — dependencies are the job_dependencies
  relation (spec A), live sidecars are mutable work-in-flight belonging
  to live discovery (live_chats/chat_live_report); stage-0 2b mapping
  table confirmed every spec name has a core counterpart and no core
  kind is lost), `target_kind` `job | chat`, `target_id` escaped path
  for path targets, RAW `agent#conversation` for delegation targets
  (never escaped: it is not a path), `\N` when unresolved, `resolved`
  bool-string, `unresolved_reason` `\N | remote | missing`.
- No pagination (bounded by reference count of one chat). Annotations:
  `root_path`, `total`.
- FK: `source_message_id` -> Message; `target_id` -> Job or Chat by
  `target_kind`.

**job_dependencies** — NEW (direct edges only).
- Inputs: `file: path (required)`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `Dependency` = composite
  `owner_job#dependency#position`, cast none.
- Fields: `owner_job` escaped path (alignment copy), `dependency`
  escaped path, `position` int-str (1-based, DECLARED order).
- No pagination. Annotations: `root_path`, `total`.
- FK: both path fields -> Job.

**job_dependencies_recursive** — NEW (recursive-closure surface;
SETTLED — direction accepted: a SEPARATE task, because option-driven
output-shape switching is cache-unfriendly in Scout and blurs the
one-table-one-relation rule; `job_dependencies` stays the unchanged
direct list).
- Inputs: `file: path (required)`, `max_depth: integer, 10`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `Dependency` = composite
  `dependency#depth`, cast none.
- Fields: `dependency` escaped path, `depth` int-str (1 = direct
  dependency of a root-owned job), `via_owner` escaped path (the owner
  that declared the edge; first in traversal order when several do).
- Semantics: BFS over job dependencies with a visited set on canonical
  dependency paths; a dependency already reported at a smaller depth is
  not repeated; equal-depth duplicates collapse to the first via_owner;
  traversal stops at `max_depth` (rows at depth == max_depth carry no
  further expansion). Cycle-safe by the visited set.
- No pagination. Annotations: `root_path`, `total`, `max_depth` is NOT
  an annotation (it is not in the settled set; it rides the Scout job
  inputs — adding it was considered and rejected to keep the annotation
  list closed).
- FK: both path fields -> Job.

**chat_role_counts** — NEW.
- Inputs: `file: path (required)`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `ChatRole` = composite
  `chat#role`, cast `:to_i` (single numeric field).
- Fields: `count` int (native).
- No pagination. Annotations: `root_path`, `total`.

### B. Message and inference tables

**chat_messages** — converted in place.
- Inputs: `file: path (required, chat file)`, `role: string, nil`,
  `page`, `per_page`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `Message`, cast none.
- Fields: `role` enumeration string, `characters` int-str, `timestamp`
  iso-or-`\N`, `large` bool-string (threshold constant unchanged).
- Paginated when `page` given; `role` filter narrows the list only.
- Annotations: pagination set + `root_path`.
- FK: key -> Message.

**chat_message** — NEW (single-message `:chat` retrieval).
- Inputs: `message_id: string (required)` (the Message id grammar; the
  chat is recovered by parsing it — no separate file input).
- Output `:chat` — the byte-exact persisted text of that ONE message
  (`Chat.print` of the message object).
- Annotations: `root_path` (escaped chat path), `first` = `last` =
  index.
- Errors: malformed id or out-of-range index raise ArgumentError (task
  layer maps to ParameterException), consistent with the existing
  message-index validation messages.

**chat_range** — converted in place.
- Inputs: `file: path (required, chat file)`, `first: integer
  (required)`, `last: integer (required)`.
- Output `:chat` — the byte-exact persisted slice. "Raw mode kept" is
  honored by making the exact-bytes form THE output (the old `raw: true`
  behavior); the `raw` INPUT is retired because it is now inherent, and
  the old envelope fields (chat/first/last) move to annotations
  (`root_path`, `first`, `last`). Recorded as a pinned detail, not a
  silent change.
- The `MAX_RANGE_MESSAGES` cap and the chat-file-only guard stay
  unchanged.

**chat_inferences** — NEW (AMENDED bout 3, C2: ROOT-scoped, tree-wide —
spec notation `chat_inferences(root)`, same family as
`chat_tool_calls(root)`; the compact DEFAULT temporal entry point
remains chat_activity_clusters, and this task is the explicit,
paginated drill-down).
- Inputs: `file: path (required, root chat or job)`,
  `max_gap_seconds: integer, 120`, `page`, `per_page`, `chat: string,
  nil` (OPTIONAL narrowing filter over the tree's chats, exactly
  chat_tool_calls' filter pattern: filters narrow the listed rows only,
  summary counts stay raw; applied at the task layer over the API's
  tree-wide list).
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `Inference` (= Message id of
  the meta message), cast none. Rows in TREE-WIDE CHRONOLOGICAL order
  (undated inferences sort last, deterministically by chat then index).
- Fields: `timestamp` iso-or-`\N`, `reasoning_present` bool-string,
  `reasoning_characters` int-str, `first_message_id` Message FK,
  `last_message_id` Message FK, `trigger_message_id` Message FK or `\N`,
  `assistant_message_id` Message FK or `\N`, `activity_cluster_id`
  cluster id or `\N` (undated inferences join no cluster; 1h/C1),
  `tool_call_count` int-str.
- Paginated when `page` given. Annotations: pagination set +
  `root_path`, `max_gap_seconds`.
- FK: key -> Inference; the four message ids -> Message;
  `activity_cluster_id` -> Activity cluster.
- Universe: the overview chats (provenance closure of the root: root
  chat plus referenced/result chats; live log chats stay OUT — they are
  mutable copies and the token evidence owns dedup semantics).

### C. Activity clusters

**chat_activity_clusters** — NEW (replaces chat_timeline's temporal
grouping role; semantic phases were already removed in phase 2).
- Inputs: `file: path (required, root chat or job)`,
  `max_gap_seconds: integer, 120`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `Cluster` (= Message id of the
  cluster's first inference), cast none. COMPACT INDEX ONLY — no member
  lists.
- Fields: `first_timestamp` iso-or-`\N`, `last_timestamp` iso-or-`\N`,
  `duration_seconds` decimal string or `\N`, `inference_count` int-str,
  `chats` multi-value escaped paths (`|`-joined, invariant 1b),
  `tool_call_count` int-str, `delegation_count` int-str.
- No pagination (bounded by cluster count). Annotations: `root_path`,
  `max_gap_seconds`, `total`, `clusters` (= total), `inferences`,
  `unclustered` (real count of undated inferences; 1h/C1).
- FK: key -> Activity cluster; `chats` -> Chat.

**chat_activity_cluster** — NEW (member detail).
- Inputs: `file: path (required, root)`, `cluster_id: string
  (required)`, `max_gap_seconds: integer, 120`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `Inference`, fields identical
  to chat_inferences' field list (one row per member inference, in
  chronological order).
- MUST consume `chat_activity_clusters` through a Scout task dependency
  and load its persisted result (`dep` + `step(:...)...load`; the
  stage-0 1f pinned pattern) so the SAME clustering computation produces
  index and members; cluster_id is validated against that result — an
  unknown id raises (ParameterException at the task layer).
- Annotations: `root_path`, `max_gap_seconds`, `total`.
- FK: as chat_inferences.

### D. Tool-call tables

**chat_tool_calls** — converted in place (tree-wide index; universe
unchanged: overview chats plus each job's live log chats, uniq).
- Inputs: `file`, `page`, `per_page`, `dedupe: boolean, false`,
  `tool: string, nil`, `agent: string, nil`, `conversation: string,
  nil`, `chat: string, nil`, `success: boolean, nil` (filters narrow
  the list only; summary counts raw — unchanged semantics).
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `ToolCall` (= call-start
  Message id), cast none.
- Fields: `output_message_id` Message FK or `\N` (no output message),
  `tool` tool_name, `call_id` provider call id or `\N`, `status`
  `success | failure | unknown`, `reason` `\N` or short controlled
  reason (never exception text), `timestamp` iso-or-`\N`,
  `start_timestamp` iso-or-`\N`, `argument_characters` int-str,
  `output_characters` int-str, `inference_id` Inference FK or `\N` (call
  belongs to no inference), `delegated` bool-string, `target_agent` or
  `\N`, `target_conversation` or `\N` (split from the delegation target
  `agent#conversation`), `copy_of` ToolCall FK or `\N` (call-start
  message id of the original), `source_kind` `primary | copy` (primary
  iff copy_of is `\N`).
- Paginated when `page` given. Annotations: pagination set +
  `root_path`, `filters` (comma-joined applied filters).
- FK: key -> Tool call; `output_message_id` -> Message; `inference_id`
  -> Inference; `copy_of` -> Tool call.

**chat_tool_call** — converted in place, REDUCED to metadata only (spec
D; recorded behavior change: the current JSON task returns full
arguments and output content — the TSV task does not; sizes and
locations replace bodies, per 1e).
- Inputs: `file: path (chat file)`, `call_index: integer (required)`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, one row, key_field `ToolCall`, field list
  identical to chat_tool_calls.
- Annotations: `root_path`, `total` (=1).

**chat_tool_call_jobs** — NEW (flat call->job table).
- Inputs: `file: path (root)`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `CallJob` = composite
  `call_message_id#escaped_job_path`, cast none.
- Fields: `job` escaped path (alignment copy).
- No pagination. Annotations: `root_path`, `total`.
- FK: key parts -> Tool call, Job.

### E. Token tables

**chat_tokens** — converted in place as the SUMMARY table (the event
list and evidence move to their own tasks; the `attribution` input is
retired in favor of chat_attribution — recorded).
- Inputs: `file: path (required)`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `Scope`, cast `:to_i` (all
  fields numeric).
- Fields: `pt`, `ct`, `tt`, `cct`, `cwt`, `rt` (native Integers). Rows:
  `deduplicated_total`, `chat_evidence`, `receipt_evidence`,
  `receipt_only` (evidence-coverage descriptions; chat_evidence and
  receipt_evidence overlap and must not be summed — only
  deduplicated_total and receipt_only compare additively; semantics
  unchanged from the core).
- No pagination. Annotations: `root_path`, `total` (=4), `conflicts`,
  `incomplete_evidence` (int counts).

**chat_token_events** — NEW (paginated event list).
- Inputs: `file`, `page`, `per_page`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `TokenEvent`, cast none
  (mixed: strings + counts).
- Fields: `pt`,`ct`,`tt`,`cct`,`cwt`,`rt` int-strings, `deduplication`
  enumeration (`inference_id | provider_response_id | lineage |
  receipt`), `conflict` bool-string, `incomplete_evidence` bool-string,
  `canonical_source` escaped path or `\N`, `canonical_origin`
  `chat_meta | agent_meta`.
- Paginated when `page` given. Annotations: pagination set +
  `root_path`.
- FK: key -> Token event; `canonical_source` -> Chat.

**chat_token_evidence** — NEW (aligned evidence rows).
- Inputs: `file: path (required)`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list` (aligned-by-construction), key_field
  `Evidence` = composite `token_event_id#occurrence` (canonical evidence
  is occurrence 1), cast none.
- Fields: `origin` `chat_meta | agent_meta`, `source` escaped path,
  `call_id` or `\N`, `tool_name` or `\N`, `meta_address` or `\N`
  (chat_meta rows), `evidence_address` or `\N`, `output_address` or
  `\N`, `agent_meta_index` int-str or `\N` (agent_meta rows).
- No pagination. Annotations: `root_path`, `total`.
- FK: key part 1 -> Token event; `source` -> Chat.

**chat_accounting** — converted in place; a DISTINCT operation from
chat_tokens (per-import accounting over the chat's closure, not
scope totals). Full field list and own/closure scope semantics as in
the section-4 retirement entry; this entry exists so section 2 covers
every task alphabetically-placeable. Post-freeze placement
clarification logged as a deviation in tmp/phase3-b2/bout2-record.md
(content unchanged from the retirement-table definition).
- Inputs: `file: path (required)`, `scope: own | closure, own`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `Chat` (own scope: one row
  per closure chat; closure scope: ONE merged row keyed by the root),
  cast none.
- Fields: `imports` multi (escaped paths), `unresolved_imports` multi,
  `messages`, `pt`,`ct`,`tt`,`cct`,`cwt`,`rt` int-strings,
  `token_events`, `conflicts`, `incomplete_evidence`, `tool_calls`,
  `direct_jobs` int-str, `direct_pt`..`direct_rt`, `direct_events`
  int-strings, `delegated_pt`..`delegated_rt`, `delegated_events`
  int-strings, `delegated_subtrees` multi (escaped paths), `warnings`
  int-str.
- No pagination. Annotations: `root_path`, `total`, `scope`.

**chat_attribution** — NEW (promoted from the retired `attribution:
true` mode).
- Inputs: `file: path (required)`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `Bucket`, cast none (bucket is
  a string).
- Fields: `pt`,`ct`,`tt`,`cct`,`cwt`,`rt` int-strings, `events`
  int-str. Rows: `root`, `delegated`, `unattributed` (semantics:
  canonical-evidence-source split, unchanged from
  ChatAnalyst.attribution).
- No pagination. Annotations: `root_path`, `total` (=3),
  `conflicts`, `incomplete_evidence` reused as quality flags, plus the
  linked/unresolved job lists are NOT cells (multi-value paths; the
  lists remain available through chat_overview/job surfaces — recorded
  simplification; `linked_jobs`/`unresolved_jobs` counts were rejected
  as annotation additions to keep the list closed).

### F. Operational tasks

**live_chats** — converted in place.
- Inputs: `file: path (required)`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `Chat` (canonical path),
  cast none.
- Fields: `mtime` iso, `age_seconds` decimal string, `size` int-str,
  `likely_active` bool-string, `source` `provenance | glob | jobs`,
  `jobs_file` escaped path or `\N` (only :jobs entries). Newest-first
  ordering preserved; the job-root status block is dropped from the
  table (it describes the ROOT, not a row; the root is addressable
  through chat_overview/job_overview) — recorded simplification.
- No pagination (bounded). Annotations: `root_path`, `total`.
- Fail-soft semantics unchanged (vanishing chats skipped).

**chat_live_report** — NEW (core live report; separate from file
discovery exactly as the spec separates them).
- Inputs: `file: path (required)`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `Entry` = `reference` (job id)
  when non-empty else escaped path, cast none.
- Fields: `kind` `inference | workload_context | agent_activity |
  dangling_job`, `path` escaped or `\N`, `state` or `\N`, `status` or
  `\N`, `chat_task` or `\N`, `agent` or `\N`, `conversation` or `\N`,
  `source` multi-value (`sidecar|agent_view|society` subset,
  `|`-joined).
- No pagination. Annotations: `root_path`, `total`.
- Fail-soft unchanged (ChatAnalyst.live wraps core fail-soft).

**inbox_state** — converted in place, INDEX ONLY (recorded behavior
change authorized by the spec: note contents move to inbox_note).
- Inputs: `file: path (required, chat save file)`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, key_field `Note` (absolute note path,
  escaped), cast none.
- Fields: `state` `pending | delivered`, `name`, `mtime` iso, `size`
  int-str.
- No pagination. Annotations: `root_path`, `total`. Missing directories
  = empty table, never error; race tolerance unchanged.

**inbox_note** — NEW (the body surface for exactly one note).
- Inputs: `file: path (required, chat save file)`, `name: string
  (required)` (plain file name).
- Output `:text` — the note's exact contents.
- Missing note raises (ParameterException at the task layer); this is a
  point read, not a discovery surface.

**post_inbox_advice** — converted in place; every safeguard kept
(chat-root guard, plain-name validation, non-empty message, reserved
`abort` name rejection before any write, no-overwrite, default
timestamped name).
- Inputs: `file`, `message: string (required)`, `name: string, nil`.
- Output `:tsv`, type `:list`, ONE row, key_field `Posted` (escaped
  posted path), cast none.
- Fields: `name`, `save_file` escaped, `inbox_dir` escaped, `size`
  int-str. The delivery-semantics prose note is dropped from the result
  (it is static boilerplate; it lives in the task desc and README) —
  recorded simplification.
- Annotations: `root_path` (= save file), `total` (=1).

## 3. Settled decisions (the two the work order required, plus pins)

1. **Null convention** (2b): `\N` sentinel in String columns; `""` =
   empty string; cast numeric columns use native empty=>nil;
   absent-trailing-cell asymmetry never relied upon. ACCEPTED as
   directed.
2. **Summary-counts placement** (2e; AMENDED bout 3, C3): split by
   natural derivation — chat_overview annotations carry
   `chats`/`jobs`/`delegations` (the overview traversal derives them
   anyway); chat_activity_clusters annotations carry
   `clusters`/`inferences`/`unclustered`. The cluster index KEEPS its
   per-cluster `tool_call_count` and `delegation_count`: clustering
   operates on inference records that already carry `tool_call_count`
   (a chat_inferences field per the spec), so the cluster count is a
   sum over members — free. The `chats` multi-value identifier list
   itself serves as the chat identification; no redundant `chat_count`
   is added. chat_overview never computes clusters. AMENDED as
   directed (the original "not added because deriving them is
   expensive" wording is superseded: once inferences carry the counts,
   the cost argument fails).
3. **Recursive dependency surface** (2f): separate task
   `job_dependencies_recursive`; flat owner->dependency rows with
   visited-set + depth cap (`max_depth`, default 10); direct list
   unchanged. ACCEPTED as directed; name pinned as
   `job_dependencies_recursive`.
4. **Boolean encoding**: `true`/`false` strings, `\N` for NULL; no
   `:to_b` exists (freeze probe A); no consumer needs native booleans.
5. **Timestamp**: UTC `iso8601(3)`, normalize-or-NULL (1d).
6. **CR escape**: `%0D` included (1a).
7. **reference_type enumeration**: confirmed with both exclusions
   (dependencies -> job_dependencies; live -> live discovery), evidence
   stage-0 2b mapping table; no core kind is lost and no spec name lacks
   a counterpart.

