## 5. Ruby API adjustment list (contract for the step-3+ bouts)

Targeted additions to lib/ChatAnalyst/api.rb (additive; no existing
method signature changes):

1. `ChatAnalyst::Ids` (THIS bout, lib/ChatAnalyst/ids.rb):
   `escape_path`/`unescape_path` (1a table), `chat_id`/`job_id`
   (canonical-path wrappers over the existing canonical behaviors —
   `canonical_chat_path` and `Chat.provenance_path(:job, ...)`),
   `message_id(chat_path, index)` / `parse_message_id(id)`,
   `composite_key(*parts)` / `parse_composite(key)`,
   `token_event_id(event)`. Malformed ids raise ArgumentError with the
   observed-message style.
2. `ChatAnalyst.inferences(root, max_gap_seconds: 120)` (AMENDED
   bout 3, C2 — root-scoped, tree-wide): inference records over the
   provenance-closure chats (the overview universe; live logs stay
   OUT), one per inference meta, in the chat_inferences field shape
   (message ids, reasoning presence/characters, tool-call count and
   delegated-call count), tree-wide chronological order (undated last,
   deterministic chat-then-index tiebreak). `activity_cluster_id` is
   NOT part of this list computation alone — callers that need it use
   activity_clusters' mapping (below); keeping the two computations
   separate lets chat_inferences run without any clustering while the
   cluster computation attaches ids to its own member records.
3. `ChatAnalyst.activity_clusters(root, max_gap_seconds: 120)`: ONE
   computation returning the compact cluster index records AND the
   message_id -> cluster_id mapping AND summary counts
   inferences/clusters/unclustered (1h model, C1 policy: only
   timestamped inferences cluster; an undated inference joins no
   cluster and influences no gap); `activity_cluster(root, cluster_id,
   max_gap_seconds)` validates the id against the same computation
   (unknown/foreign-scope ids raise ArgumentError at this layer;
   ParameterException mapping happens at the task layer) and returns
   member inference records in chronological order. Task layer wires
   the dep+load reuse.
4. `timeline_call_records` gains `inference_id` (Message id of the
   owning inference; nil when the call belongs to none) and
   `source_kind` derivation; `tool_calls`/`tool_call` records expose
   them; target_agent/target_conversation split from
   delegation_target.
5. Clustering helper shared by 2-3 with the C1 policy (adjacent-gap
   comparison over TIMESTAMPED inferences only; undated inferences are
   excluded from runs and from gap computation).
6. No changes to tokens/attribution/live/overview semantics — TSV
   conversion is task-layer serialization over the existing shapes.

